; The P3.5 host-link wire format: one OCaml definition of the serial frame layouts, codes,
; payloads and CRC, plus the software codec host code uses to build requests and read
; responses (host_link_migration.md HL2, p3.5-hardware-loader.md).
;
; Its own library for the same reason isa/ is: lib/'s Hardware_loader and host software
; must read the same numbers, and host software must not link Hardcaml to get them. It
; sits beside isa/, not inside it, because serial framing is not instruction encoding;
; neither library depends on the other.
;
; Note the absence of `hardcaml` and of every protemu library. The wire format is bytes
; and their meanings. The independent Verilog peer (tinytapeout/test/p3_loader_tb.v) keeps
; its own copy on purpose and is never generated from this one.

(library
 (name protemu_host_link_wire)
 (public_name hardcaml_protemu.host_link_wire)
 (libraries core)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_jane))
 (lint
  (pps ppx_js_style)))
